True open-source licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, GPL, AGPL, etc.) allow anyone —
including commercial vendors and the U.S. Government — to run, modify, and
often sell the software free of charge.

That is intentionally NOT the arrangement for WokeNet.

This repository is SOURCE-AVAILABLE under a STRICT dual license designed for:

  • VALIDATION & TRANSPARENCY — anyone can read, audit, test, and verify
  • VALUE CAPTURE — commercial and government production use requires payment

  (A) Limited Non-Commercial Evaluation & Audit License  — free, narrow
  (B) Commercial & Government Production License         — paid / written

If you need rights broader than Section A, you must obtain Section B.
There is no implied production license from GitHub visibility.

